00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MAY 3 2006\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer.\r Absent: Wolfson.\r Staff: Ball, Coroalles, Levin, Lysik, Parker, Peirce, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Charles Caspary.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian to approve the agenda with a revision to the title of Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Wolfson was absent.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Washburn introduced Charles Caspary, Las Virgenes Water Management District, who presented children�s books to the City of Calabasas regarding water conservation. Mayor Washburn presented a proclamation to Dr. Stephen Trudeau, Program Director of Stirling Behavioral Health Institute, declaring May as Mental Health Month. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian spoke regarding the upcoming Fine Arts Festival that will be taking place on May 6 and 7, 2006. Councilmember Maurer announced an upcoming Blood Drive that will be occurring at Chaparral Elementary School.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Brian Cameron, Calabasas, The Oaks Homeowners Association, spoke regarding bus service that is not being utilized by the residents of the association. Merideth Hasson, Calabasas, spoke in support of the City enacting an ordinance to require low-flow toilets and gas shut-off valves for homes that are being sold.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of the minutes for the April 19, 2006 City Council meeting. \r\r Waive further reading and adopt Ordinance No. 2006-223, approving ZCH-004-005 for the subdivision of one parcel into two parcels, rough grading of one pad and driveway on one resulting parcel, and development of one single-family home including a pool/spa, horse stable/corral area, septic system, driveway, and retaining walls and dedication of 8.7 acres of permanent open space on the second resulting property located at 24135 Mulholland Highway (APN�s: 4455-006-012, -013).\r\r Request for the City to quitclaim 1,210 square-foot portion of real property known as Pansy Drive located in the Calabasas Highlands. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1016, authorizing enforcement of Section 21107.7 of the California Vehicle Code to specific roads within the Oaks of Calabasas (Tract 35596). \r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to approve Items #1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 with Councilmember Groveman�s ABSTENTION on Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Wolfson was absent.\r\r\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r \r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1021, approving documents related to the refinancing of the CFD 2001-1 Special Tax Assessment Bonds and the execution and delivery of the not-to-exceed $30,000,000.00 Special Tax Refunding Bonds, Series 2006. \r\rGary Lysik, Chief Financial Officer, provided the staff report.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman to adopt Resolution 2006-1021, approving documents related to the refinancing of the CFD 2001-1 Special Tax Assessment Bonds and the execution and delivery of the not-to-exceed $30,000,000.00 Special Tax Refunding Bonds, Series 2006. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Wolfson was absent.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Discussion of pole-mounted banner signs.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\rThe City Council directed staff to refer the issue of pole-mounted banner signs to the Planning Commission and return to the City Council with a recommendation for action. \r\r Discussion of Community Development 2-year work plan.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\rDouglas Brownstone, Calabasas Highlands, spoke regarding problems with development in the Calabasas Highlands.\r\rThe City Council received the report and provided direction to staff.\r\r Recommendation to award 19 contracts for landscape maintenance of the common areas within individual homeowner associations & common benefit areas within Landscape Maintenance District 22, Specification 05-06-02, to Venco Western Landscape. \r\rSteve Ball, Landscape Maintenance Manager, provided the staff report.\r\rDan Scully, Calabasas, Henry Cespedes, Calabasas, and Pat Van Atta, Las Villas Homeowners Association, spoke in support of the approval of the contracts.\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to staff�s recommendation to approve 19 contracts for landscape maintenance. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Wolfson was absent.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of April 13, 2006 to April 20, 2006. \r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Mayor Washburn provided an update on the Headwaters Corners Task Force.\r\rRECESS TO CALABASAS EDUCATION FUND BOARD OF DIRECTORS MEETING\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested a progress update of the Headwaters Center and update on stormwater watershed issues. \r\rADJOURN \r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:10 p.m. in memory of Ed Davis.\r\r\r\r____________________________________ \rGwen Peirce, Assistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 3 -\u0015\r05/03/06\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00